    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65544" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεγᾰρ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <u>Megarian</u>, <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Ach.</u>
			522
		</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεγαρικοὶ κέραμοι</span>, and
		in the language of trade <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεγαρικά</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Megarian pottery</i>,
				Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1205
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μαγαρικός</span>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεγαρικοί, οἱ</span>,
				<i>philosophers of the Megarian school</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1046b29
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				2.106
			</span></i>; οἱ M. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαλεκτικοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1.279
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>; M. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρωτήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chrysipp.Stoic.
					2.90
				</span></i>
			: fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεγαρίς</span></b>  (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>), <i>Megarian
			territory</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.31
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
